hange the properties  of mikola's blood to potentially give  the blood the ability to create flames  and burn away any burdens the body May  hold I see this process as being  extremely painful this could be where  they sleeping properties of Saint Trina  who is widely discussed to also be  mikola started from for him to be able  to just sleep through this process to  somehow bear the pain and torture that  comes with it sort of like anesthesia  but I think we'll have to talk about  this in another video the saint Trina  Laura runs very deep so keep on the  lookout for that this is all a major  stretch I understand that there isn't  much we understand about mikola at this  point if he did do all of this that I'm  suggesting then he didn't let anyone in  the halog tree know of his plan and he  definitely didn't let Melania know what  he was doing either he went on a rampage  through the lands between defying mikola  which ultimately ended in a stalemate  between her and radon and yes I say it  was a stalemate she had to be carried  back to the Haley Tree by one of her  Knights after she nuked the continent of  Khalid and even then she couldn't kill  radon and yet she still refers to  herself as undefeated which I guess is  technically true if you discount a tie  in there there is a lot of holes in this  Theory but I think it's fun to think of  different intentions with the demigods  and especially mikola since we know so  little about him but I think it's clear  that mikola had a dream to help those  burdened in the world whether they were  his own family or not but what he's  become when we find him here in mowgun's  Palace I have to believe is a far  stretch from what he was before just  like most things throughout the lands  between this is what I meant when I said  that this mikola is not the same mikola  from all the descriptions and stories we  read about him I think when we do meet  him in a future DLC we won't be met with  an imperial child who seeks to help u